    <briefdescription>
<para>Edition-aware access control for LLM Wiki plugin. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Enforces that the LLM Wiki plugin and certain features are only available in enterprise, hyperscaler, and military editions. Community and minimal builds return <computeroutput>PermissionDenied</computeroutput> for plugin operations.</para>
<sect1 id="edition__gate_8h_1autotoc_md6_1s1"><sect2 id="edition__gate_8h_1autotoc_md6">
<title>Compile-time gating</title><para>Define <computeroutput>THEMISDB_LLM_WIKI_ENTERPRISE_ENABLED</computeroutput> when building enterprise+ editions:</para>
<para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">cmake<sp/>-DTHEMISDB_LLM_WIKI_ENTERPRISE_ENABLED=ON<sp/>&lt;build_dir&gt;</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
</sect2></sect1>
<sect1 id="edition__gate_8h_1autotoc_md7_1s1"><sect2 id="edition__gate_8h_1autotoc_md7">
<title>Feature-level gating</title><para>Sub-features like <computeroutput>"llm_wiki_wikipedia"</computeroutput> (Wikipedia dump ingestion) require explicit license keys in addition to edition checks.</para>
</sect2></sect1>
<sect1 id="edition__gate_8h_1autotoc_md8_1s1"><sect2 id="edition__gate_8h_1autotoc_md8">
<title>Runtime behavior</title><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Community/minimal: All plugin calls return <computeroutput>Status::PermissionDenied()</computeroutput></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Enterprise/hyperscaler/military: Full plugin functionality</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Wikipedia sub-feature: Additional license key check</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="version"><para>1.0.0 (Phase 3 hardening) </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
</sect2></sect1>
